<title>GERMANY: Bonn to top up Series 121 Bobl by 2 bln dmk.</title>
<headline>Bonn to top up Series 121 Bobl by 2 bln dmk.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government will top up its Series 121 five-year Bundesobligationen (Bobl) bonds by two billion marks to 14 billion marks, the Bundesbank as issuing agent said on Friday.</p>
<p>The additional volume will be placed via German stock exchanges from March 12, the Bundesbank said.</p>
<p>Separately, the government increased the yield on its Series 122 Bobl issue to 4.52 percent from 4.43 percent by lowering the issue price to 99.90 from 100.30.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
